# ZFS root: the module is rebuilt with every dist-kernel update, in the same emerge transaction and before the new initramfs (a kernel update without it leaves
# a ZFS-root machine with an initramfs that has no zfs.ko). Same lines as sys-apps/horcrux-core ships for installed machines (/etc/portage/package.use/horcrux-core).
# Since OpenZFS 2.4 the kernel module is part of sys-fs/zfs itself (USE=modules); sys-fs/zfs-kmod is retired (masked by sys-apps/horcrux-core).
sys-fs/zfs rootfs dist-kernel modules
